', '<p>Phil Ivey opens up for the first time about his poker strategy and teaches you how to make smarter moves at the table.</p>', NULL, 'free', NULL, 'free', NULL, 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pzqjv5WJerA', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3723, NULL, '/courses/3761/', '/courses/3761', '2022-05-09 01:38:33'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:48'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
INSERT INTO public.courses (wp_id, status, slug, title, content, excerpt, short_description, price_type, price, access_mode, certificate_id, intro_video, materials_enabled, menu_order, steps_source, step_counts, featured_image_id, cover_image_id, old_path, new_path, published_at, modified_at) VALUES (3783, 'publish'::public.course_status, 'masterclass-robin-roberts-teaches-effective-and-authentic-communication', 'Masterclass: Robin Roberts Teaches Effective and Authentic Communication', '
<p>Millions of people spend their mornings with Robin Roberts, one of today’s most beloved broadcasters. Now the Emmy-winning “Good Morning America” co-anchor is sharing how she creates unforgettable moments through human connection. Learn how to communicate effectively, whether it’s in front of an audience, at work, or with those you love. Start embracing vulnerability, building resilience, and living life with optimism.</p>



<p><strong>Instructor(s)</strong>: Robin Roberts<br><strong>Class Length</strong>: 11 video lessons (2 hrs 22 min)<br><strong>Category</strong>: Communication Skills<br><strong>Course Materials</strong>:  <a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1VpZZ0gEv6REqnI77o2NJQJwvyVbkpPQW" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Class Workbook.pdf</a></p>



<h3 id="h-would-you-like-to-donate-to-the-luthas-center-for-excellence">Would you like to donate to the Luthas Center for Excellence?</h3>



<img alt="" border="0" src="https://www.paypal.com/en_US/i/scr/pixel.gif" width="1" height="1">




<p><strong>Course Lessons:</strong></p>



<ol><li>Meet Your Instructor<br>15:56<br>Emmy-winning “Good Morning America” co-anchor Robin Roberts welcomes you to her class, where she will teach you about negotiating, effective public speaking, body language, and how to authentically connect with your audience.</li><li>Make Your Mess Your Message<br>12:26<br>Robin explains what “make your mess your message” means to her and how it can help you. She also tells deeply personal stories about her cancer diagnosis and treatment.</li><li>Sharing and Embracing Vulnerability<br>11:24<br>Robin believes that vulnerability is strength. With archival footage of some of her most raw moments on camera—including during Hurricane Katrina—Robin shows you the power of being vulnerable.</li><li>Making an Authentic Connection<br>7:55<br>Connection starts with a genuine interest in people. Robin shares how going back to the basics, including good manners, helps you connect with people.</li><li>Public Speaking<br>09:15<br>If you’re going to speak in public, Robin recommends that you know your audience, don’t rely on a script, and use some power poses.</li><li>Interviewing for a Job<br>16:00<br>Robin walks you through her strategies for getting the job you want, including bringing ideas, being sincere, and asking for advice.</li><li>Communicating Your Value at Work<br>11:34<br>How do you make the most out of your situation at work? Robin encourages you to know your worth, focus on standing out, find allies, and more.</li><li>Behind-the-Scenes at Good Morning America<br>11:35<br>Get an intimate look at the inner workings of “Good Morning America” as Robin shares a day on set.</li><li>Communicating for Television<br>10:32<br>Robin reveals her approach to communicating for TV, including focusing on storytelling, letting your authenticity shine, and choosing people over process.</li><li>Interviewing People for TV<br>17:42<br>Robin breaks down some of her most memorable interviews, including with Selma Blair, President Barack Obama, and First Lady Michelle Obama.</li><li>Living Life With Optimism and Resiliency<br>17:58<br>Robin imparts some of her most poignant lessons about building optimism, how to change the way you feel, and how to enjoy the process.</li></ol>



<p></p>
', '<div>
<div>Robin Roberts teaches you her techniques for powerful communication, building strength from vulnerability, and connecting with any audience.</div>
</div>', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/ZQuSpFaQFgM', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3734, NULL, '/courses/3783/', '/courses/3783', '2022-03-15 13:41:23'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:49'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
INSERT INTO public.courses (wp_id, status, slug, title, content, excerpt, short_description, price_type, price, access_mode, certificate_id, intro_video, materials_enabled, menu_order, steps_source, step_counts, featured_image_id, cover_image_id, old_path, new_path, published_at, modified_at) VALUES (3781, 'publish'::public.course_status, 'masterclass-samuel-jackson-teaches-acting', 'Masterclass: Samuel Jackson Teaches Acting', '
<p>As a kid, Samuel L. Jackson stuttered so badly that he stopped talking for almost a year. Today he’s one of the world’s most successful actors, with roles in over 100 films, including Pulp Fiction and The Avengers. In his online acting class, the Oscar-nominated star shares how he creates memorable characters, powerful performances, and a long-lasting career. Learn to master auditions, analyze scripts, and find the truth in every role you play.</p>



<p><strong>Instructor(s)</strong>: Samuel Jackson<br><strong>Class Length</strong>: 21 video lessons (5 hrs 0 min)<br><strong>Category</strong>: Arts &amp; Entertainment<br><strong>Course Materials</strong>: <a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1tLs4MiS9p_TMZsYPf_b_WF20O1Ew0B3l" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Class Workbook.pdf</a></p>



<p><strong>Course Lessons:</strong></p>



<ol><li>Introduction<br>03:36<br>You know Samuel L. Jackson from iconic films like Pulp Fiction and Die Hard with a Vengeance. Now he’s your acting teacher. Sam shares his goals for his MasterClass, as well as his mindset toward acting: it’s an adventure.</li><li>Creating Characters<br>20:37<br>Learn how Sam imbues every role with a sense of purpose and complexity of character—even if they only appear on screen for a few minutes. In this lesson, he shares the fundamentals of his characterization process.</li><li>Physical Characterization<br>12:32<br>Sam dives deep into the myriad ways actors can use their bodies to reflect their characters’ personalities. Learn how to use posture, gait, voice, and physical appearance to add complexity to your characters.</li><li>Case Study: Caveman''s Valentine<br>10:56<br>Sam breaks down the nuances of his characterization process and performance as Romulus, a prodigal but schizophrenic and homeless concert pianist, in The Caveman’s Valentine.</li><li>Student Session: Breaking Down a Script - Part 1<br>15:27<br>Sam directs student actors in a workshop, and the first scene on the docket is the iconic diner scene from Pulp Fiction. In this lesson, Sam helps them break down the script to gain a deeper understanding of the characters’ intentions.</li><li>Student Session: Breaking Down a Script - Part 2<br>16:43<br>Get inside Jules’s head as Sam breaks down the Ezekiel passage and walks the students through the different ways the character could perform the scene.</li><li>Student Session: Character Biographies<br>15:10<br>Creating in-depth character backstory is an integral part of Sam’s process. He pushes the students to develop a connection with Jules by imagining his life story and how he got to this moment in the diner.</li><li>Student Session: Make It Your Own<br>08:10<br>One of the student actors puts a unique spin on Jules, showing that there are many “right” ways to create characters.</li><li>Voice &amp; Character<br>19:48<br>Sam reveals how his childhood experiences have informed his approach to character voices throughout his career, and discusses his method of developing a vocalization plan.</li><li>Student Session: Plumb Your Emotional Depths<br>13:28<br>Sam directs the actors to perform a scene from The Negotiator in which two characters—Danny and Farley—are on opposite ends of the power spectrum. Students play the scene and then switch roles.</li><li>Student Session: Use Your Voice, Use Your Body<br>21:56<br>Sam analyzes the students’ choices of power positions when playing Danny and how movement and stillness can each convey power in a different way. He shows how posture works on each side of the phone as each character is pushed to their limits.</li><li>Working With Directors<br>12:24<br>Learn Sam’s tried-and-true methods for developing strong working relationships with directors.</li><li>On-Set Collaboration<br>13:13<br>Sam describes the movie set environment as “a moving circus.” Learn his code of on-set conduct, which has earned him respect throughout the industry as a true professional.</li><li>Student Session: Developing Characterization<br>21:05<br>On the surface, this Kingsman scene is a simple conversation between two characters. The actors’ task is to dig deeper, access the subtext of the exchange, and create characters who will make the otherwise “bland” dialogue more interesting.</li><li>Student Session: Making Bold Choices<br>14:48<br>When it comes to characterization, it’s better to show up with too much rather than not enough. Sam pushes the student actors to take risks and commit to their choices.</li><li>Enriching Your Acting Practice<br>10:54<br>Sam encourages you to nurture a sense of curiosity and explore stories set in worlds that you are unfamiliar with, so that you have a more expansive view of the characters you take on throughout your acting career.</li><li>Auditioning<br>13:18<br>Don’t walk into a casting room thinking about the job; go in with the goal of demonstrating your skill as an actor. Sam gives you this and more time-tested rules for auditioning.</li><li>Growing Your Acting Career<br>20:28<br>Sam walks you through the most important business relationships you’ll form as an actor, and offers wisdom on how to best work with them.</li><li>Sam''s Journey From New York to Hollywood<br>19:04<br>Learn how Sam got “plucked” from the Negro Ensemble Company, where he performed alongside Denzel Washington and Morgan Freeman, to go to Hollywood.</li><li>Hollywood Lessons<br>09:28<br>Sam shares three very personal lessons learned over the decades he’s spent in Hollywood.</li><li>Conclusion<br>07:17<br>When you finish this MasterClass and continue your career in acting, Sam urges you to remember your responsibility to your audience—and to the world at large.</li></ol>
', '<p>One of the most successful actors of our generation teaches you how to elevate your acting.</p>', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/C7Osh7kitFM', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3733, NULL, '/courses/3781/', '/courses/3781', '2022-03-15 17:05:04'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:49'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
INSERT INTO public.courses (wp_id, status, slug, title, content, excerpt, short_description, price_type, price, access_mode, certificate_id, intro_video, materials_enabled, menu_order, steps_source, step_counts, featured_image_id, cover_image_id, old_path, new_path, published_at, modified_at) VALUES (3775, 'publish'::public.course_status, 'masterclass-serena-williams-teaches-tennis', 'Masterclass: Serena Williams Teaches Tennis', '
<p>Serena Williams, the world''s #1 ranked women''s tennis player and winner of 23 Grand Slam singles titles, teaches you tennis and reveals the secrets of her game. This is as close as you can get to a private lesson with one of the world''s greatest tennis players.</p>



<p><strong>Instructor(s)</strong>: Serena Williams<br><strong>Class Length</strong>: 9 video lessons (2 hrs 00 min)<br><strong>Category</strong>: Arts &amp; Entertainment<br><strong>Course Materials</strong>:  <a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1CNlxyfCmtQVHglUbKauKwQB_lJlq7yTR" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Class Workbook.pdf</a></p>



<div class="wp-block-group">
<p class="has-text-align-center"><strong>Donate to the Luthas Center</strong> </p>



<div class="wp-block-buttons">
<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://cash.app/$DameLuthas">CashApp</a></div>



<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://www.paypal.com/donate/?hosted_button_id=KV3MZ7EJ8Y5SW">Paypal</a></div>



<div class="wp-block-button"><a class="wp-block-button__link" href="https://account.venmo.com/u/DameLuthas" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Venmo</a></div>
</div>
</div>



<p><strong>Lesson Plans:</strong></p>



<ol><li>Introduction - Focus and Desire<br>02:46<br>Whether you’re a beginner or a budding champion, Serena Williams can teach you how to improve your game on and off the court.</li><li>Groundstrokes I<br>13:00<br>Consistency is key in tennis. Experience the drills Serena’s father ran for her as a kid—drills she still runs every day as a pro.</li><li>Mastering Groundstrokes<br>10:17<br>Master baseline play with advanced footwork, backhand and troubleshooting techniques that Serena uses to challenge any opponent.</li><li>Controlling The Court<br>13:12<br>Serena teaches you how to turn defense into offense, when to anticipate and react, and how to open up the court for easy winners.</li><li>Mental Toughness<br>16:36<br>Serena Williams believes that tennis is 70% mental. Learn how to dig deep in tough situations from a player known for impossible comebacks.</li><li>Advanced Net Play<br>08:39<br>Serena rarely comes to the net, but when she does, she makes it count. Learn proper approach, volley, and smash techniques.</li><li>Training Like a Pro<br>14:50<br>The average women’s professional tennis match lasts two hours, but Serena trains to play all-out for four. Here she reveals her tips for staying in top shape, her pro drills, and how to keep it fun while putting in the hard work.</li><li>Preparing for Game Day<br>11:40<br>Serena starts a big match before she even steps out onto the court. Learn the physical and mental routines that take Serena to the Grand Slams over and over again.</li><li>Making Of A Winner<br>12:08<br>Serena’s run of titles is otherworldly, but it all started with goals, heroes, and a lot of practice.</li><li>Mastering The Serve<br>17:16<br>Serena’s serve is legendary. Weaponize your serve as Serena teaches you the mechanics that power 128mph of pure genius.</li></ol>
', '<div class="row no-gutters d-flex flex-column justify-content-center align-items-center">
<div class="row d-flex justify-content-center mc-mt-1">
<p class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-7">Step up your game with two hours of the techniques, drills, and mental skills that made Serena the best in the world.</p>
</div>
</div>', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tZzh0T9LjP0', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3730, NULL, '/courses/3775/', '/courses/3775', '2022-03-23 02:42:37'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:49'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
INSERT INTO public.courses (wp_id, status, slug, title, content, excerpt, short_description, price_type, price, access_mode, certificate_id, intro_video, materials_enabled, menu_order, steps_source, step_counts, featured_image_id, cover_image_id, old_path, new_path, published_at, modified_at) VALUES (3805, 'publish'::public.course_status, 'masterclass-shonda-rhimes-teaches-writing-for-television', 'Masterclass: Shonda Rhimes Teaches Writing for Television', '
<p>When Shonda Rhimes pitched Grey’s Anatomy she got so nervous she had to start over. Twice. Since then, she has created and produced TV’s biggest hits. In her screenwriting class, Shonda teaches you how to create compelling characters, write a pilot, pitch your idea, and stand out in the writers’ room. You’ll also get original pilot scripts, pitch notes, and series bibles from her shows. Welcome to Shondaland.</p>



<p><strong>Course Length</strong>: 6hrs 25min</p>



<p><strong>Course Materials</strong>: Provided</p>



<ul><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=108cOG8lMZUZXi1B82zjKIyZFYqMc7sgW" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Class Workbook.pdf</a></li><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1CBrNdhl8OEtiHFSyL_XGgcUteuVIXiw2" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Grey''s Anatomy Original Pitch.pdf</a></li><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1s-m_wYwDFNR2DJb6Fi2K0fkW3hDaANTE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Grey''s Anatomy Pilot.pdf</a></li><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1LLSNaN1Or2ZTnd9bTjmAhltlutfNrADs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Grey''s Anatomy Story Bible.pdf</a></li><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1a4Q7AwXhmthlJASK9yFcwGv6ebNrYq9D" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Scandal 301 Script.pdf</a></li><li><a href="https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&amp;id=1uVIdcOSwtZdUzQhAUn9KxLk7uYclB2PJ" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Scandal Pilot</a></li></ul>



<p><strong>Note</strong>: Courses are not visible on mobile devices at this time</p>



<h3 id="h-would-you-like-to-donate-to-the-luthas-center-for-excellence">Would you like to donate to the Luthas Center for Excellence?</h3>



<img alt="" border="0" src="https://www.paypal.com/en_US/i/scr/pixel.gif" width="1" height="1">




<p><strong>Lesson Plan</strong></p>



<ol><li>Introduction<br>05:00<br>Welcome to Shondaland. Meet Shonda, the woman behind some of television''s biggest and most talked about hits, and learn what she''ll teach you about the craft of writing for television.</li><li>Teach Yourself TV Writing<br>11:16<br>Shonda discusses the importance of knowing your television history and how you can learn some of the fundamentals of storytelling on your own.</li><li>Finding an Idea<br>14:15<br>It all begins with an idea. Shonda reveals her process for finding and assessing ideas, and determining what makes a great idea for a TV series.</li><li>Developing the Concept<br>12:21<br>Show titles, story bibles, tone, structure - Shonda walks you through how to take your idea and turn it into a fully-fleshed out concept.</li><li>Researching Your Story<br>16:15<br>Effective research can make your story come to life. Using case studies from Scandal and Grey''s Anatomy, Shonda discusses her techniques and method for conducting research for her stories.</li><li>Creating Memorable Characters: Part 1<br>18:07<br>Meredith Grey, Olivia Pope, Cristina Yang - Shonda has created some of the most memorable characters to grace television. In this chapter, Shonda breaks down how she approaches the character development process.</li><li>Creating Memorable Characters: Part 2<br>16:43<br>Shonda shares her techniques on how to effectively develop and evolve your characters when writing your stories, including when and how to kill off characters.</li><li>Pitching Your Show<br>17:33<br>You can''t make a TV show without pitching it first. Shonda shares how she originally pitched Grey''s Anatomy to network executives and her top tips for how to deliver an effective pitch.</li><li>Writing a Script: Structure<br>8:29<br>Shonda breaks down the five acts of television and what needs to be accomplished in each one to tell an effective story in a one-hour drama.</li><li>Writing a Script: Process<br>9:16<br>You have your premise, your characters, and your research. Now it''s time to write your script. Shonda talks about her own process for preparing to write a script, including how to create beat sheets and outlines.</li><li>Writing a Script: Effective Habits<br>11:52<br>Writer''s block? No time? Shonda breaks through the myths of writing and details how exactly she gets her writing done.</li><li>Writing a Script: The Pilot<br>12:21<br>When it comes to television, the pilot is everything. Shonda discusses the key ingredients to what makes a great pilot, including discussing her alternative opening scenes for the show Scandal.</li><li>Writing Authentic Dialogue<br>08:46<br>Shonda shares her tips on how to write realistic and engaging dialogue for your characters.</li><li>Case Study: Grey''s Anatomy Pilot - Part 1<br>12:55<br>Shonda breaks down the Grey''s Anatomy pilot act-by-act and shares why she made certain story decisions.</li><li>Case Study: Grey''s Anatomy Pilot - Part 2<br>14:29<br>Shonda continues to break down the Grey''s Anatomy pilot act-by-act.</li><li>Case Study: Scandal Pilot - Act One<br>14:42<br>Shonda breaks down the first act of the Scandal pilot, revealing why she structured the opening scene the way she did.</li><li>Case Study: Scandal Pilot - Act Two<br>10:03<br>Shonda discusses act two of the Scandal pilot and the introduction of Olivia''s White House storyline.</li><li>Case Study: Scandal Pilot - Act Three<br>16:28<br>Shonda discusses act three of the Scandal pilot and how to balance various story lines in a single episode.</li><li>Case Study: Scandal Pilot - Act Four<br>16:44<br>Shonda discusses act four of the Scandal pilot and the importance of quickening the pace of your action.</li><li>Case Study: Scandal Pilot - Act Five<br>19:54<br>Shonda discusses the final act of the Scandal pilot and reveals how she set up the pilot for an entire season of episodes.</li><li>Editing Your Script<br>19:02<br>You''ve written the first draft - now comes the task of editing your script. Shonda reveals her own editing process and provides tips on the best things to cut in a script.</li><li>Beyond the Pilot: Writing a Series<br>13:27<br>Shonda has never had a TV show last for less than six seasons. In this chapter, Shonda discusses what keeps people watching a show beyond the pilot.</li><li>Scandal Case Study: "It''s Handled"<br>10:48<br>In this case study, Shonda discusses how the scene between Olivia and Rowan Pope in the season three premiere of Scandal cleverly uses dialogue to reveal who the characters are, and the importance of the scene in the show''s story.</li><li>Breaking into the Industry<br>13:06<br>Shonda reveals her top tips for networking, working entry-level jobs, and her thoughts on film school.</li><li>Working in a Writers’ Room<br>11:35<br>Shonda discusses what she looks for in writers when staffing her shows and how her own writers'' rooms are structured.</li><li>Working in TV Production<br>11:34<br>Shonda talks about how a writer can best adapt to the fast-paced world of television production and the important lessons she has learned in over a decade of producing TV.</li><li>Showrunning<br>16:43<br>Becoming and being a showrunner is exciting, but it comes with immense responsibilities. Shonda talks through how she learned to become an effective showrunner.</li><li>Life of a Writer<br>08:07<br>Writing is not just a profession; it is a way of life. Shonda discusses the issue of "work/life balance" and the physical and mental habits to survive a writer''s life.</li><li>Shonda''s Journey<br>12:38<br>Learn how Shonda went from being a Dartmouth and USC graduate to the queen of Thursday night.</li><li>Conclusion<br>01:27<br>Shonda wraps up her MasterClass with a few departing thoughts and suggestions for next steps.</li></ol>



<p></p>
', '<div class="ember-view classroom-layout-panel-layout-main__module">
<div class="classroom-workspace-overview__description t-16">
<div class="row no-gutters d-flex flex-column justify-content-center align-items-center">
<div class="row d-flex justify-content-center mc-mt-1">
<p class="col-12 col-md-8 col-lg-7">When Shonda Rhimes pitched Grey’s Anatomy she got so nervous she had to start over. Twice. Since then, she has created and produced TV’s biggest hits. In her screenwriting class, Shonda teaches you how to create compelling characters, write a pilot, pitch your idea, and stand out in the writers’ room. You’ll also get original pilot scripts, pitch notes, and series bibles from her shows. Welcome to Shondaland.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ember-view classroom-layout-panel-layout-main__module"> </div>', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/efU0GWksItg', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3745, NULL, '/courses/3805/', '/courses/3805', '2022-02-26 15:21:25'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:51'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
INSERT INTO public.courses (wp_id, status, slug, title, content, excerpt, short_description, price_type, price, access_mode, certificate_id, intro_video, materials_enabled, menu_order, steps_source, step_counts, featured_image_id, cover_image_id, old_path, new_path, published_at, modified_at) VALUES (3793, 'publish'::public.course_status, 'masterclass-spike-lee-teaches-independent-filmmaking', 'Masterclass: Spike Lee teaches Independent Filmmaking', '
<p>Spike Lee didn’t just direct his award-winning 1986 feature debut, She’s Gotta Have It. He was also the writer, star, truck driver, location scout, electrician, and caterer, because that’s what it took to get his film made.</p>



<p><strong>Course Length</strong>: 3hrs 11min</p>



<p><strong>Course Materials</strong>: Provided</p>


<!-- wp:wpcp/useyourdrive-block {"shortcode":""} /-->


<p><strong>Note</strong>: Courses are not visible on mobile devices at this time</p>



<h3 id="h-would-you-like-to-donate-to-the-luthas-center-for-excellence">Would you like to donate to the Luthas Center for Excellence?</h3>



<img alt="" border="0" src="https://www.paypal.com/en_US/i/scr/pixel.gif" width="1" height="1">




<p><strong>Masterclass Lesson Plan:</strong></p>



<p>1. Introduction<br>04:30<br>Meet your new instructor, writer/director/producer/professor—Spike Lee. Spike explains what he hopes you’ll gain from his class: the tools of film grammar—or visual storytelling—and the DIY spirit to make your own original, independent films.</p>



<p>2. Putting Words On Paper<br>16:56<br>Spike provides you with a blueprint of his writing process to help you write your script. Learn his index card technique, his disciplined writing practice, and his advice for writing with a partner.</p>



<p>3. Storytelling<br>11:06<br>Spike teaches you his techniques for writing bold, distinct characters, capturing two sides of a story, and creating stories that react to social injustice.</p>



<p>4. Speaking Truth to Power: On the Waterfront<br>09:40<br>Breaking down the director’s choices in one of his favorite films, Elia Kazan’s On the Waterfront, Spike demonstrates how cinema can be a powerful tool for speaking the truth.</p>



<p>5. Spike''s Film 101s Pt. 1<br>07:35<br>Learn Spike’s tips for creating realistic budgets and shooting schedules (and sticking to them), working on location, and how to make your crew feel appreciated.</p>



<p>6. Case Study: Financing Malcolm X<br>07:00<br>Spike recounts his battle to secure additional funds for Malcolm X to show you how self-reliance, self-determination, and dedication to your story can help finance a project.</p>



<p>7. Importance of Casting<br>20:36<br>“The wrong actors, the wrong roles could turn out the wrong movie.” Spike shares his tips for successful casting and his experiences casting some of his most infamous roles.</p>



<p>8. Collaborating With Your Director of Photography<br>08:59<br>Learn what to look for in a director of photography, including how to “audition” a DP and how to create a plan of action, once you’ve found the right collaborator.</p>



<p>9. Storytelling with Camera Coverage<br>10:43<br>Spike walks you through the iconic camera angles and techniques that have come to define his visual style. Then, he breaks down how he uses each to increase tension and heighten the drama.</p>



<p>10. Storyboards: Malcolm X<br>03:49<br>Using his original storyboards for the assassination scene in Malcolm X, Spike illustrates the construction of a scene, and the level of detail required to create the illusion of chaos.</p>



<p>11. Spike''s Film 101s Pt. 2<br>08:18<br>For Spike, the take is a sacred moment. Learn his rules for managing your crew and running a set effectively in order to deliver the best possible takes.</p>



<p>12. Directing Actors<br>10:44<br>How can you inspire the best performance from your actor? Spike teaches his techniques for directing your actors with sensitivity and respect, including how to communicate and establish trust.</p>



<p>13. Collaborating and Improvising with Actors<br>10:13<br>Spike believes that a good director both commands and surrenders to the moment. Using scenes from He Got Game and School Daze, he shares tips on how to harness improvisational moments and adjust to story changes on-the-fly.</p>



<p>14. Opening Title Sequences<br>11:47<br>Analyzing opening title sequences from Mo’ Better Blues, 25th Hour, and BlacKkKlansman, Spike teaches the art of establishing tone in the first few minutes of your film.</p>



<p>15. Music Is Key<br>14:17<br>Spike shares his strategies for enhancing drama through music. Learn his advice for working with a composer, turning source into score, and using music as a counterpoint.</p>



<p>16. Editing<br>17:05<br>By taking a look at the inter-cutting technique in BlacKkKlansman, Spike demonstrates how he was able to create heightened drama and tonal balance in pivotal scenes.</p>



<p>17. Film as an Agent of Change<br>08:31<br>Spike discusses the filmmaker’s responsibility to bring diversity to the film industry—both on screen and behind the scenes.</p>



<p>18. Storytelling for Documentaries<br>06:48<br>Examining his powerful nonfiction films When the Levees Broke and 4 Little Girls, Spike shares insights on how to handle true stories with passion and respect.</p>



<p>19. Closing</p>
', '<p>Spike Lee didn’t just direct his award-winning 1986 feature debut, She’s Gotta Have It. He was also the writer, star, truck driver, location scout, electrician, and caterer, because that’s what it took to get his film made. I.</p>', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'open', NULL, 'https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/grybwMU_uIU', TRUE, 0, 'lesson_course_id_fallback', '{"lessons":1,"topics":0,"quizzes":0}'::jsonb, 3739, NULL, '/courses/3793/', '/courses/3793', '2022-03-05 12:56:35'::timestamptz, '2022-07-27 02:27:50'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (wp_id) DO UPDATE SET status = EXCLUDED.status, slug = EXCLUDED.slug, title = EXCLUDED.title, content = EXCLUDED.content, excerpt = EXCLUDED.excerpt, short_description = EXCLUDED.short_description, price_type = EXCLUDED.price_type, price = EXCLUDED.price, access_mode = EXCLUDED.access_mode, certificate_id = EXCLUDED.certificate_id, intro_video = EXCLUDED.intro_video, materials_enabled = EXCLUDED.materials_enabled, menu_order = EXCLUDED.menu_order, steps_source = EXCLUDED.steps_source, step_counts = EXCLUDED.step_counts, featured_image_id = EXCLUDED.featured_image_id, cover_image_id = EXCLUDED.cover_image_id, old_path = EXCLUDED.old_path, new_path = EXCLUDED.new_path, published_at = EXCLUDED.published_at, modified_at = EXCLUDED.modified_at;
